# Generate Calculator Variant Pages

When the user says "生成变体页面" or similar, follow this automated workflow.

## Step 0: Read Plan & Pick Next Batch

1. Read `.cursor/plans/variants.json`
2. Find the first batch with `"status": "pending"`
3. Use that batch's data (baseCalculator, variants array) as the work target
4. Announce: "Generating variants for: [baseCalculator] ([N] variants)"

## Step 1: Create Variants Data File

Create `src/lib/variants/[baseCalculator].ts`:

```typescript
export interface CalculatorVariant {
  slug: string;
  title: string;
  description: string;
  defaults: Record<string, string>;
  intro: string;
  tips: string[];
}

export const [name]Variants: CalculatorVariant[] = [
  // For each variant in the plan batch:
  {
    slug: "[from plan]",
    title: "[from plan]",
    description: "[unique 120-155 char SEO description for this specific scenario]",
    defaults: { /* from plan */ },
    intro: "[2-3 sentences unique to THIS scenario — specific market context, typical buyer profile, or financial considerations]",
    tips: [
      // 3-5 tips specific to THIS variant's numbers
      "[specific dollar amounts and percentages relevant to this scenario]",
      "[comparison to other options relevant to this price point/scenario]",
      "[actionable advice specific to this situation]",
    ],
  },
];
```

CRITICAL: Each variant MUST have unique `intro` and `tips` content. Do NOT use the same text with different numbers substituted.

## Step 2: Modify Base Calculator Component

Update the base calculator in `src/app/calculators/[baseCalculator]/[Name]Calculator.tsx`:

1. Add `defaults?: Record<string, string>` to component props
2. Use `defaults?.fieldName || "defaultValue"` in useState initializers

Example:
```typescript
interface Props {
  defaults?: Record<string, string>;
}

export function MortgageCalculator({ defaults }: Props) {
  const [homePrice, setHomePrice] = useState(defaults?.homePrice || "350000");
  const [downPayment, setDownPayment] = useState(defaults?.downPayment || "70000");
  // ...
}
```

## Step 3: Create Variant Route

Create `src/app/calculators/[baseCalculator]/[variant]/page.tsx`:

```typescript
import type { Metadata } from "next";
import { notFound } from "next/navigation";
import Link from "next/link";
import { getCalculator } from "@/lib/calculators";
import { site } from "@/lib/site";
import { [Name]Calculator } from "../[Name]Calculator";
import { [name]Variants } from "@/lib/variants/[baseCalculator]";
import { CategoryIcon } from "@/components/Icons";

interface Props {
  params: Promise<{ variant: string }>;
}

export async function generateStaticParams() {
  return [name]Variants.map((v) => ({ variant: v.slug }));
}

export async function generateMetadata({ params }: Props): Promise<Metadata> {
  const { variant: slug } = await params;
  const variant = [name]Variants.find((v) => v.slug === slug);
  if (!variant) return {};
  return {
    title: variant.title,
    description: variant.description,
    openGraph: { title: `${variant.title} | ${site.name}`, description: variant.description },
  };
}

export default async function VariantPage({ params }: Props) {
  const { variant: slug } = await params;
  const variant = [name]Variants.find((v) => v.slug === slug);
  if (!variant) notFound();
  const calc = getCalculator("[baseCalculator]")!;

  return (
    <div className="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-8 sm:px-6">
      <nav className="mb-6 text-sm text-ink-500">
        <Link href="/" className="hover:text-brand-600">Home</Link>
        <span className="mx-2">/</span>
        <Link href={`/calculators/${calc.slug}`} className="hover:text-brand-600">{calc.shortTitle}</Link>
        <span className="mx-2">/</span>
        <span className="text-ink-700">{variant.title}</span>
      </nav>

      <div className="mb-8 flex items-start gap-3">
        <div className="flex h-10 w-10 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-brand-50 text-brand-600">
          <CategoryIcon name={calc.slug} />
        </div>
        <div>
          <h1 className="text-3xl font-bold text-ink-900">{variant.title}</h1>
          <p className="mt-2 text-lg text-ink-600">{variant.description}</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div className="mb-6 rounded-lg border border-brand-200 bg-brand-50 p-4">
        <p className="text-ink-700">{variant.intro}</p>
      </div>

      <div className="rounded-xl border border-ink-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-card sm:p-8">
        <[Name]Calculator defaults={variant.defaults} />
      </div>

      <div className="mt-8">
        <h2 className="text-xl font-bold text-ink-900">Key Considerations</h2>
        <ul className="mt-4 space-y-3">
          {variant.tips.map((tip, i) => (
            <li key={i} className="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span className="mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand-500" />
              <span className="text-ink-700">{tip}</span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>

      {/* Related variants */}
      <div className="mt-8 border-t border-ink-200 pt-6">
        <p className="text-sm font-medium text-ink-600">See also:</p>
        <div className="mt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
          {[name]Variants.filter((v) => v.slug !== slug).slice(0, 4).map((v) => (
            <Link key={v.slug} href={`/calculators/[baseCalculator]/${v.slug}`}
              className="rounded-md border border-ink-200 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm text-ink-600 hover:border-brand-300 hover:text-brand-600">
              {v.title}
            </Link>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>

      <div className="mt-6">
        <Link href={`/calculators/${calc.slug}`} className="text-sm font-medium text-brand-600 hover:text-brand-800">
          &larr; Back to {calc.title}
        </Link>
      </div>
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Step 4: Update Sitemap

Add variant URLs to `src/app/sitemap.ts`:

```typescript
import { [name]Variants } from "@/lib/variants/[baseCalculator]";

// In the function, add:
const [name]VariantPages = [name]Variants.map((v) => ({
  url: `${base}/calculators/[baseCalculator]/${v.slug}`,
  lastModified: new Date(),
  changeFrequency: "monthly" as const,
  priority: 0.7,
}));
```

## Step 5: Verify Build

```bash
npm run build
```

Confirm all variant pages appear in the route list.

## Step 6: Commit & Push

```bash
git add -A && git commit -m "Add [baseCalculator] variant pages ([N] scenarios)" && git push
```

## Step 7: Update Plan Progress

Update `.cursor/plans/variants.json`: change the batch's status from `"pending"` to `"done"` and add `"completedAt": "[ISO date]"`.

## Critical Rules

1. Each variant MUST have unique editorial content (intro + tips) — not just different numbers
2. The `intro` should mention market context, buyer profile, or scenario-specific considerations
3. The `tips` must contain specific dollar amounts calculated for THAT variant's defaults
4. Do not create more than 7 variants per batch — quality over quantity
5. All internal links between variants use relative paths
6. NO emoji anywhere
